{"key": "e16ad0b313a1b5fe5f963a639119a8595bf69c5a5e16a80f295548ab841b5cd7", "input": {"format": "json", "source_type": "official_transcript", "selector": null, "encoding": null, "cached_pages": null, "cache_file_key": null, "country_iso3": "RWA", "year": 2021, "source_sha256": "b56b9a0d63ebce5e08488f76e06c65fc5dc8ef0f080653fbb1e41151117d4e37", "adapter_version": "1.2-canonical-transcript-locators"}, "blocks": [["• Excellency, Abdulla Shahid, President of the General Assembly", {"paragraph": 1, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 4, "bbox": [152.0, 123.14, 445.62, 136.61], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["• Excellency, Secretary-General António Guterres", {"paragraph": 2, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 5, "bbox": [152.0, 141.54, 380.23, 155.01], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["• Excellencies, Heads of State and Government", {"paragraph": 3, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 6, "bbox": [152.0, 159.93, 366.69, 173.4], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["• Distinguished Delegates", {"paragraph": 4, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 7, "bbox": [152.0, 178.33, 274.24, 191.8], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["Fighting the COVID-19 pandemic has challenged the international system like never before.", {"paragraph": 5, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 8, "bbox": [123.36, 196.73, 493.57, 222.59], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["However, alongside unfortunate examples of inequality, we have also seen evidence of the spirit of global solidarity and fairness, exemplifying the best values of our organisation.", {"paragraph": 6, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 9, "bbox": [123.36, 227.52, 493.6, 265.78], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["The COVAX mechanism, despite its limitations, is one such case. Without this system, Africa’s vaccine deficit would be even more severe.", {"paragraph": 7, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 10, "bbox": [123.36, 270.71, 493.6, 296.58], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["But we can and must do more, to speed up vaccine distribution in Africa. Doing so benefits the entire world.", {"paragraph": 8, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 11, "bbox": [123.36, 301.5, 493.58, 327.37], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["The positive steps from various partners and companies toward building local vaccine manufacturing capacity is also very welcome.", {"paragraph": 9, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 12, "bbox": [123.36, 332.3, 493.56, 358.16], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["We must harness this positive momentum to build long-term pandemic resilience, where it is needed most.", {"paragraph": 10, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 13, "bbox": [123.36, 363.09, 493.61, 388.96], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["The cooperation at the G-7 and G-20 to issue new Special Drawing Rights is another positive example.", {"paragraph": 11, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 14, "bbox": [123.36, 393.88, 493.52, 419.75], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["A further voluntary reallocation of new SDRs to countries that need them most, will help create the fiscal space required for a faster and more equitable recovery from the pandemic.", {"paragraph": 12, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 15, "bbox": [123.36, 424.68, 493.6, 462.94], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["Nevertheless, the world is seriously off-track with the Sustainable Development Goals, as highlighted during today’s Food Systems Summit.", {"paragraph": 13, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 16, "bbox": [123.36, 467.87, 493.57, 493.73], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["In fairness, we were behind schedule with the SDGs even before the pandemic hit. But there is now increased attention to figuring out how to refocus our efforts, and catch up.", {"paragraph": 14, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 17, "bbox": [123.36, 498.66, 493.55, 536.92], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["We need to convert this sense of urgency into a durable political commitment to achieving the SDGs.", {"paragraph": 15, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 18, "bbox": [123.36, 541.85, 493.63, 567.72], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["That commitment must put climate change mitigation at the centre of our efforts.", {"paragraph": 16, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 19, "bbox": [151.71, 572.64, 490.99, 586.11], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["The severity of weather-related disasters is increasing year-by-year.", {"paragraph": 17, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 20, "bbox": [151.71, 591.04, 446.25, 604.51], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["We cannot afford for the result of COP-26 in November to be inconclusive or divisive.", {"paragraph": 18, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 21, "bbox": [123.36, 609.44, 493.6, 635.3], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["We also need to re-emphasize the importance of citizen-centred governance and accountability.", {"paragraph": 19, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 22, "bbox": [123.36, 640.23, 493.6, 666.1], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["This not only guarantees well-being and material progress, but also security, stability, and confidence in the future.", {"paragraph": 20, "pdf_page": 45, "pdf_block": 23, "bbox": [123.36, 671.02, 493.58, 696.89], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["The extremist ideologies that drive terrorism and genocide must be named, identified early, and dismantled, without ambiguity or hesitation.", {"paragraph": 21, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 2, "bbox": [123.36, 83.65, 493.52, 109.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["On that, we cannot afford to play politics.", {"paragraph": 22, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 3, "bbox": [151.71, 113.65, 333.39, 127.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["I wish to conclude with a strong endorsement of the Secretary-General’s report on Our Common Agenda.", {"paragraph": 23, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 4, "bbox": [123.36, 131.65, 493.56, 157.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["The Secretary-General is right to warn of a possible breakdown in the multilateral system, in the face of the Covid pandemic, worsening conflict, the climate emergency, and chronic poverty.", {"paragraph": 24, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 5, "bbox": [123.36, 161.65, 493.63, 199.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["This would have disastrous consequences for all of us, and the risk should be taken seriously.", {"paragraph": 25, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 6, "bbox": [123.36, 203.65, 493.56, 229.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["The Secretary-General’s Action Plan merits our full support, particularly the need for a global vaccination plan, a renewal of trust between governments and citizens, more focus on the needs of youth, and a rejuvenated commitment to factbased reasoning and science.", {"paragraph": 26, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 7, "bbox": [123.36, 233.65, 493.57, 283.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["Whether we are able to convene physically for the 77th General Assembly in 2022, or for the Secretary-General’s proposed Summit of the Future, depends on the actions we all take in the coming months.", {"paragraph": 27, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 8, "bbox": [123.36, 287.65, 493.62, 325.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["With determination and focus, it can be achieved.", {"paragraph": 28, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 9, "bbox": [151.71, 329.65, 368.39, 343.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}], ["Thank you for your kind attention.", {"paragraph": 29, "pdf_page": 46, "pdf_block": 10, "bbox": [151.71, 347.65, 302.72, 361.12], "origin_file": "data/unga_general_debate_verbatim_en/UNGA76_2021/A_76_PV_4_EN.pdf", "origin_sha256": "082b55bb5f3874a905ce88927cc0e6dbe51bde0664418124fc4251c19cd52e14"}]]}